 # Review Stabilized Work Log
 
+## 2026-10-03 - Price lookup returns a quote only for the symbol asked for
+
+- ENGINEER (Claude, separate thread). Operator approved this as the next
+  separate patch. Independent of the multi-symbol series in its code.
+- Defect: `tick_reader.get_best_bid_ask_last(venue, symbol)` fell back to the
+  snapshot's venue-level row when the symbol had no tick. The publisher fills
+  that row with the first symbol it fetched, so the caller received another
+  symbol's quote. SHOWN in the paper history (audit findings 30, 32): eleven
+  fills across five symbols at one price; XRP/EUR fills at a BTC price.
+  Reproduced by test: with the old lookup a paper market order for ADA/EUR
+  fills from a snapshot that holds only a BTC/USDT tick.
+- Change: the fallback and its helper are removed; a symbol with no tick of
+  its own has no snapshot quote. The reader now matches symbols with the
+  publisher's own spelling rule (`symbol_router.normalize_symbol`: case, dash
+  or slash), so a spelling difference the fallback used to hide still
+  matches. `PaperEngine._price` no longer lets a failed exchange fetch escape,
+  because that fetch is now the normal path for a symbol with no tick and the
+  paper runner does not catch it around `evaluate_open_orders`.
+- One existing test asserted the fallback
+  (tests/test_market_snapshot_readers.py, venue-row-only snapshot returns a
+  quote); it now asserts None. No producer of a snapshot without a tick list
+  exists in the repository; only that test fixture had the shape.
+- Effect on each caller when a symbol has no tick (reviewer traced, SHOWN
+  unless noted): strategy runner and paper engine fetch that symbol from the
+  exchange, or get no price when `use_ccxt_fallback` is off; paper market
+  orders are refused `market_quality:no_reference_price`; the live local gate
+  price is None and the intent stays pending `missing_local_quote`; shadow
+  fills record nothing; last-price provider and price probe report no quote.
+- NOT fixed, operator decision needed: `market_quality_guard.check` returns
+  ok with reason `no_quote_data` when it has no quote, unless
+  `block_when_unknown` is set (default false; the strict template sets it).
+  Before this change the guard checked the wrong symbol's spread; now it
+  checks nothing. A LIMIT intent for a symbol with no tick therefore reaches
+  submission with no spread check, on the paper and live paths. Pinned by a
+  test in both settings.
+- NOT fixed, noted: the live intent consumer estimates zero notional for a
+  market intent with no quote and consumes a daily trade slot before the
+  router rejects it; `multi_venue_view.venue_rows` raises NameError before and
+  after; venue aliases (`gate` vs `gateio`) still do not match.
+- Operator note: the publisher's symbol list comes from the environment and
+  defaults to BTC/USD; `config/trading.yaml` lists BTC/USDT first. A symbol
+  the publisher does not publish now gets no snapshot quote.
+- Reviewer subagent returned ACCEPT WITH FIXES. Fixed after it: the paper
+  price-fetch crash path, symbol spelling, and six test gaps it found by
+  mutation. Fixes not re-reviewed.
+- VERIFIED_ENV (cloud clone, Python 3.11.15): seven affected test files =>
+  110 passed; the new tests fail on the old lookup; 14 of 14 mutations
+  fail a test (bytecode caching off); 75-scenario single-symbol differential
+  identical; full suite 4015 passed, 19 failed, the same 19 that fail on
+  unmodified master here.
+- UNVERIFIED: Python 3.12, CI, end-to-end live intent paths, Hetzner
+  environment and publisher symbol list. HIGH risk (shared by paper and live
+  price paths). Not pushed, not deployed. READY_FOR_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW.
+
